.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "OS Assignment" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount
function reads the file associated with
.I file
and counts its lines, words, and characters.
The resulting counts are stored in the variables pointed to by
.IR lines ,
.IR words ,
and
.IR chars .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success and -1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mygrep (3)
